What “Data Trust” is (one sentence)
Data Trust is AskDB’s data reliability control room: it runs automated checks on your warehouse, rolls them into a trust score (0–100), and shows what is wrong, how serious it is, and which dashboards/chat answers depend on that data.

In the app: sidebar Data Trust → route /data-quality (Reliability Center UI).

What a “monitor” is
A monitor is a data-quality rule the platform runs on a schedule (when you Run checks or refresh). Each monitor:

Targets a dataset (e.g. sales transactions, claims).
Checks something concrete (missing values, duplicates, stale data, invalid codes, etc.).
Has a pass threshold (e.g. “at least 99% of rows must pass”).
Maps to a quality dimension (Completeness, Timeliness, Validity, …).
Contributes to the overall trust score and shows as passing / failing with optional sample failures.
There are two kinds:

Type	Who defines it	Can delete?
Built-in rules
Shipped per industry (automotive / insurance) — reconciliations, freshness, volume, cross-table checks
No — admins enable/disable or tune threshold/owner
Custom monitors
Admins create via New monitor
Yes — only custom ones
Custom monitors do not accept free-form SQL; the server builds read-only checks from a safe template (column must exist on the dataset catalog). That limits risk and keeps checks consistent.

How monitors help the business
Early warning — Problems surface in Data Trust before executives see wrong KPIs or AI gives confident answers on bad data.
Single trust score — One number plus bands (Excellent / Good / Fair / Risk) and 6 dimensions (Accuracy, Completeness, Consistency, Timeliness, Validity, Uniqueness), each with a plain question (e.g. “Is the data refreshed within its agreed SLA?”).
Prioritization — Severity (critical → low) and owner so teams know who acts.
Traceability to use cases — Built-in datasets are tagged with where data is used (e.g. Executive cockpit, Revenue dashboard, AI Chat answers), so leaders see why a failing rule matters.
Trend — Score and dimension trends over time (e.g. 7-day delta on the hero).
Operational detail — Freshness table, schema drift, entity/catalog changes, alerts, drill-down on a rule.
Important distinction for leadership: The trust % on an individual AI Chat answer is a separate, answer-level score (semantic match, SQL path, empty results). Data Trust monitors govern warehouse quality; they do not replace per-answer trust, but they reduce the chance that chat and dashboards run on bad data.

Monitor types (what you can add)
When an admin clicks New monitor, they choose a kind (UI labels):

Kind	Business meaning	Example
Required values (not_null)
Column must be filled
Every sales row has a dealer
No duplicates (unique)
Business key unique
order_id not repeated
Value range (range)
Min/max business limits
total_sales ≥ 0
